    "title": "Where Floaters Refresh: A River Site's Comeback Story - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By McKenzie River Reflections ,\n1 days ago NIMROD: Lane County this week celebrated improvements the 47-acre Eagle Rock riverfront property that was heavily damaged in the 2020 Holiday Farm wildfire. The property, acquired by the county in 1979 from a private landowner, came with deed restrictions requiring that any development serve elderly visitors and remain accessible to people of all abilities, according to Lane County Parks Manager Brett Henry. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
